## The AUDIT mechanism / existing audit-line code

**`AuditOwnerCreated.java`** (`.../rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java`) is the sole audit emission point. It writes a single line to a dedicated SLF4J logger literally named `"AUDIT"`. There is **no** `Audit` class/interface/bean — auditing is done entirely through this named logger.

```java
public class AuditOwnerCreated {

    private static final Logger AUDIT = LoggerFactory.getLogger("AUDIT");

    public void service(@Val Owner owner) {
        AUDIT.info("Owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={} membershipLevel={} membershipNumber={}",
                owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate(),
                MembershipLevel.of(owner), membershipNumber(owner));
    }

    private static String membershipNumber(Owner owner) {
        if (owner.getCustomerCode() == null || owner.getRegistrationDate() == null) {
            return null;
        }
        return owner.getCustomerCode() + "-M"
                + String.format("%02d", FiscalYear.of(owner.getRegistrationDate()) % 100);
    }
}
```

Key point: the current emission is a **human-readable audit line only**. It does NOT emit the structured `OWNER_CREATED` event with `seq`/`ownerId`/`event` fields that the acceptance test expects (see tests below). The line uses `MembershipLevel.of(owner)` (recomputed) rather than the stored `owner.getMembershipLevel()`.

